<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine tax revenue up in Aug to $3.71 bln.</title>
<headline>Argentine tax revenue up in Aug to $3.71 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine government collected $3.71 billion in tax revenue in August, up 10.6 percent from August 1995, the Economy Ministry said Monday.</p>
<p>The largest increase came in collection from the value-added tax. VAT revenue rose 16.1 percent to $1.68 billion in August from $1.45 billion in August 1995.  </p>
<p>Income tax was 8.1 percent higher at 513 million.</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0618</p>
